1
00:00:01,127 --> 00:00:03,379
Announcer: They've got
to stop them in this series.

2
00:00:05,173 --> 00:00:06,966
- Geez! - Come on!
- Damn it!

3
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:09,760
Adult Sheldon:
In Texas, the holy Trinity

4
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:13,973
is god, football and barbeque,

5
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:16,559
not necessarily in that order.

6
00:00:16,893 --> 00:00:21,105
I don't care if you win,
just cover the damn spread.

7
00:00:21,314 --> 00:00:22,394
Mom, are you betting again?

8
00:00:22,565 --> 00:00:23,565
No.

9
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:24,877
Announcer: Fans on their feet,

10
00:00:24,901 --> 00:00:26,044
trying to urge the defense on.

11
00:00:26,068 --> 00:00:27,195
Fourth down.

12
00:00:27,403 --> 00:00:28,446
Gotta punt.

13
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:29,654
Gotta.

14
00:00:29,906 --> 00:00:32,200
Statistically, always
punting on fourth down

15
00:00:32,408 --> 00:00:33,408
makes no sense.

16
00:00:33,576 --> 00:00:35,161
Statistically,
you're a dumb-ass.

17
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:35,995
Hey.

18
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:37,538
When the aggies give up the ball

19
00:00:37,747 --> 00:00:39,373
on their own five-yard line,

20
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:42,960
the opposing team has
a 92% chance of scoring.

21
00:00:43,169 --> 00:00:45,049
When they punt from deep
in their own territory,

22
00:00:45,087 --> 00:00:48,549
the other team still has
a 77% chance of scoring.

23
00:00:48,758 --> 00:00:49,800
But since they convert

24
00:00:50,009 --> 00:00:52,678
on fourth down 50% of the time,

25
00:00:52,887 --> 00:00:55,348
the math says they should
never punt again.

26
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:01,354
Okay, you can tell me,
who's his real daddy?

27
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:06,400
Sheldon, I've been playing and
coaching football all my life.

28
00:01:06,651 --> 00:01:07,985
I don't think your math
is right.

29
00:01:08,486 --> 00:01:09,529
Really?

30
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:11,030
Hang on.

31
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:12,864
No, it's right.

32
00:01:12,949 --> 00:01:14,593
Announcer: Able to hold a&m
to a field goal,

33
00:01:14,617 --> 00:01:16,077
they'll only be down six points.

34
00:01:16,285 --> 00:01:17,453
Is it your dentist?

35
00:01:17,662 --> 00:01:19,080
The little guy with the glasses?

36
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:20,665
You can tell me.

37
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:24,460
J” nobody else
is stronger than I am j”

38
00:01:24,669 --> 00:01:27,380
j" yesterday I moved a mountain j”

39
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:29,924
j" I bet I could be your hero j”

40
00:01:30,132 --> 00:01:32,760
j" I am a mighty little man j“

41
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:36,264
j" I am a mighty little man. J“

42
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:43,813
I got to tell you, I'm a little
worried about my mother.

43
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:45,661
She keeps betting on
these football games,

44
00:01:45,856 --> 00:01:47,616
next thing you know,
there's an Italian fella

45
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:49,735
driving off with
her pickup truck.

46
00:01:53,281 --> 00:01:54,321
You think Sheldon's right?

47
00:01:54,574 --> 00:01:55,658
About what?

48
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:58,035
The punting and the math.

49
00:01:58,786 --> 00:01:59,912
I should think so.

50
00:02:00,121 --> 00:02:02,123
He's been doing our taxes
since he's six years old.

51
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:03,457
We never been audited.

52
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:05,293
That's true.

53
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:10,881
He even got us that
nice refund last year.

54
00:02:11,841 --> 00:02:17,847
J” I got some ocean front
property in Arizona... j”

55
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:20,474
how come mom's
not taking me to school?

56
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,100
'Cause once in a while,

57
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:24,312
your dad wants to spend
some time with you.

58
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,730
My little shel-man.

59
00:02:27,523 --> 00:02:29,317
But mom's car has a backseat.

60
00:02:29,525 --> 00:02:31,068
Statistically,
I'm much safer there.

61
00:02:31,277 --> 00:02:33,112
Hey, I'm glad you brought up
statistically.

62
00:02:33,321 --> 00:02:35,615
You think those numbers you
talked about for Texas a&m

63
00:02:35,823 --> 00:02:37,325
would apply to my jv squad?

64
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:39,327
I don't see why not.

65
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:43,497
Unlike our former principal,
math doesn't discriminate.

66
00:02:45,041 --> 00:02:47,121
You're not thinking about
taking his advice, are you?

67
00:02:47,293 --> 00:02:49,378
- Never you mind.
- But he's wrong.

68
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:51,464
Everybody knows
you punt on fourth down.

69
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:54,258
Why does everybody knowing
something make it right?

70
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:55,885
Because.

71
00:02:58,262 --> 00:03:00,348
That's what makes
this country great.

72
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:02,200
Adult Sheldon: Many years later,

73
00:03:02,224 --> 00:03:04,185
my brother would use
this same argument

74
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:06,020
in front of a judge.

75
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:09,315
He was still convicted
for urinating in a phone booth.

76
00:03:21,744 --> 00:03:23,287
Oh, damn it.

77
00:03:23,496 --> 00:03:24,696
I'll send in the punting team.

78
00:03:24,914 --> 00:03:25,914
Hang on. Hang on.

79
00:03:26,082 --> 00:03:27,082
What?

80
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,543
Let's go for it.

81
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:31,587
Why? We got plenty of time.

82
00:03:31,796 --> 00:03:33,756
I know. Still want to go for it.

83
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:37,051
We're on the 12-yard line.
Everybody know you punt.

84
00:03:37,259 --> 00:03:39,470
Why does everybody knowing
something make it right?

85
00:03:42,098 --> 00:03:44,475
But we're on
the 12-yard line, coach.

86
00:03:46,769 --> 00:03:49,313
Okay, coach says
we're going for it.

87
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:50,898
Stupid brother.

88
00:03:51,107 --> 00:03:52,692
- What?
- Nothing.

89
00:03:53,109 --> 00:03:55,653
- Power left jumbo on two, on two. Ready?
- All: Break!

90
00:03:56,404 --> 00:03:59,156
P.A. announcer: And your wolves
are going for it on fourth down.

91
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,367
What the hell? Punt!

92
00:04:01,826 --> 00:04:03,953
Statistically, they're
better off going for it.

93
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:06,497
- Says who?
- My little boy.

94
00:04:13,838 --> 00:04:15,214
That's why everybody punts.

95
00:04:15,423 --> 00:04:17,007
That was just plain foolishness.

96
00:04:17,425 --> 00:04:19,260
Your little boy's a real genius.

97
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:21,220
Well, actually he is.

98
00:04:24,974 --> 00:04:27,393
Too many men on
the field, defense.

99
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:28,853
Replay fourth down.

100
00:04:29,061 --> 00:04:31,605
Ah. Thank you, Jesus.

101
00:04:31,814 --> 00:04:33,774
Now, can I send in
the punt team?

102
00:04:37,403 --> 00:04:38,403
Coach?

103
00:04:39,989 --> 00:04:41,073
Break!

104
00:04:43,284 --> 00:04:44,636
Announcer: And they're
going for it again.

105
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,203
What the hell? Punt!

106
00:04:46,412 --> 00:04:48,292
Remind me to tell you about
the tax refund I got

107
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:49,707
from the IRS.

108
00:04:50,291 --> 00:04:51,291
Set. Hut!

109
00:04:56,672 --> 00:04:58,424
Go, go, go, go, go, go!

110
00:05:00,509 --> 00:05:01,510
- Go!
- Whoo!

111
00:05:03,012 --> 00:05:05,181
Go, go, go! Go!

112
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:07,349
Announcer:
He's at the 30, the 20, the 10.

113
00:05:07,558 --> 00:05:09,769
Touchdown, wolves!

114
00:05:13,606 --> 00:05:15,816
I never had any doubt, coach.
Never had any doubt.

115
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:21,113
Oh, booyah! Yes.

116
00:05:21,322 --> 00:05:22,656
J'j'

117
00:05:30,956 --> 00:05:32,333
Sweet dreams, baby.

118
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:33,709
Mwah.

119
00:05:34,043 --> 00:05:35,711
Night, meemaw.

120
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:39,882
Can I ask you a favor?

121
00:05:40,341 --> 00:05:42,426
- Sure. What?
- You know those statistics

122
00:05:42,635 --> 00:05:44,275
that you were talking about
with your dad?

123
00:05:44,428 --> 00:05:48,015
Could... could that be
applied to, say,

124
00:05:48,224 --> 00:05:50,559
who might win the
cowboys-packers game next week?

125
00:05:50,768 --> 00:05:53,896
And, more specifically,
by how much?

126
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:58,067
I suppose with enough data
I could make a reasonable guess.

127
00:05:58,275 --> 00:06:00,402
I don't want a guess,
I want to know.

128
00:06:00,611 --> 00:06:01,880
Mom said you're not
supposed to gamble.

129
00:06:01,904 --> 00:06:02,947
Sleep, child!

130
00:06:03,447 --> 00:06:05,449
- Mary: Mom?
- In here!

131
00:06:05,658 --> 00:06:07,658
I'll get those
numbers to you tomorrow.

132
00:06:08,953 --> 00:06:11,163
Just tucking him in.

133
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:15,251
I got something for you.

134
00:06:16,752 --> 00:06:18,295
It's dirty.

135
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:20,923
Well, that's 'cause
it's the game ball.

136
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:23,425
And you earned it,
'cause you helped us win.

137
00:06:24,468 --> 00:06:26,303
Okay, but can you wash it?

138
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:29,890
Sheldon, your daddy's
telling you he's proud of you.

139
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:32,893
I see. Thank you, dad.

140
00:06:33,811 --> 00:06:34,895
You're welcome.

141
00:06:37,648 --> 00:06:39,316
I'm still never touching that.

142
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:41,443
Let's go wipe it off.

143
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:48,468
- - Adult
Sheldon: For the next five weeks,

144
00:06:48,492 --> 00:06:51,161
I continued to help
my father apply statistics

145
00:06:51,370 --> 00:06:52,788
to coach his team.

146
00:06:52,997 --> 00:06:55,207
Not surprisingly,
they continued to win,

147
00:06:55,416 --> 00:06:58,252
which changed my status
in the school dramatically.

148
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,580
- Yo, Sheldon!
- There he is!

149
00:07:00,838 --> 00:07:01,505
Shehdog!

150
00:07:01,714 --> 00:07:02,798
Math man!

151
00:07:03,549 --> 00:07:05,968
Hey, cutie.

152
00:07:06,719 --> 00:07:07,719
It was a nightmare.

153
00:07:07,887 --> 00:07:09,430
Shel-dog! Woo-hoo!

154
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:12,516
Hugging, hair tousling,
high fives.

155
00:07:12,725 --> 00:07:16,061
And as my popularity grew,
so did my time aloft.

156
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:20,232
J'j'

157
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,611
J” everybody wants you. J”

158
00:07:32,578 --> 00:07:35,623
Hey, I've been looking
all over for you.

159
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:37,750
Do you know how popular we are?

160
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:39,501
- We?
- Yeah.

161
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:42,171
I put the word out I was helping
you with the football stats.

162
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:43,881
And since I'm Asian,
they bought it.

163
00:07:44,423 --> 00:07:46,133
Well, I'm glad
you're enjoying it.

164
00:07:47,301 --> 00:07:48,010
You're not?

165
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:51,096
I was touched 82 times
this afternoon.

166
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:52,556
What do you mean, "touched"?

167
00:07:52,765 --> 00:07:54,141
Not inappropriately.

168
00:07:54,350 --> 00:07:55,434
Joyfully.

169
00:07:55,643 --> 00:07:57,061
Affectionately.

170
00:07:57,269 --> 00:07:59,438
A cheerleader hugged me
to her bosom.

171
00:07:59,647 --> 00:08:00,856
That's amazing.

172
00:08:02,191 --> 00:08:03,400
No more high fives.

173
00:08:03,609 --> 00:08:05,235
I can't keep washing my hands.

174
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,117
Hey.

175
00:08:13,535 --> 00:08:15,371
There's my little
assistant coach.

176
00:08:15,579 --> 00:08:16,914
Heho, dad.

177
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:19,959
You have any more,
uh, arithmetic ideas

178
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:21,335
for next week's game?

179
00:08:21,543 --> 00:08:23,879
I do, but I'm trying
to finish my homework.

180
00:08:25,589 --> 00:08:26,589
Ah.

181
00:08:29,176 --> 00:08:30,511
Looks complicated.

182
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,180
Advanced chemistry. It's not.

183
00:08:34,223 --> 00:08:35,432
What are you guys doing?

184
00:08:35,891 --> 00:08:37,786
Your brother and I are gonna
knock around a few ideas

185
00:08:37,810 --> 00:08:39,186
for the freeport game.

186
00:08:39,895 --> 00:08:40,895
Can I help?

187
00:08:41,146 --> 00:08:42,690
Actually, yeah.
Run out to my truck.

188
00:08:42,898 --> 00:08:44,334
There's a little, uh,
pocket calculator

189
00:08:44,358 --> 00:08:45,359
on my front seat.

190
00:08:45,651 --> 00:08:46,819
I got you a present.

191
00:08:47,653 --> 00:08:49,253
Thought it might help
with your figuring.

192
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:51,699
I don't need a calculator, dad.
I am one.

193
00:08:52,408 --> 00:08:53,033
Sure.

194
00:08:53,242 --> 00:08:54,242
Well...

195
00:08:54,994 --> 00:08:56,161
Go get it anyway.

196
00:08:57,871 --> 00:08:59,415
It's solar-powered.

197
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:01,291
Can you imagine that?

198
00:09:20,144 --> 00:09:22,354
Georgie, turn that down!

199
00:09:22,563 --> 00:09:23,563
What?

200
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:30,487
And look at this room.
You need to clean this mess up.

201
00:09:30,696 --> 00:09:32,031
I'll get to it later.

202
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:33,407
No, you'll get to it now.

203
00:09:33,615 --> 00:09:34,867
I don't feel like it.

204
00:09:35,284 --> 00:09:37,286
Well, your feelings have
nothing to do with it.

205
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:38,829
And stop throwing that ball.

206
00:09:39,038 --> 00:09:41,290
My room bothers you so much,
you clean it.

207
00:09:43,625 --> 00:09:46,086
Mary: That's it!
You are grounded! You hear me?!

208
00:09:46,295 --> 00:09:47,295
The hell?

209
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:51,175
Hey...

210
00:09:51,383 --> 00:09:52,509
There's my little moonpie.

211
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:55,387
Did you get a chance to look
at this week's games for me?

212
00:09:55,596 --> 00:09:58,724
- Not yet.
- You understand there's a little time crunch involved.

213
00:09:58,932 --> 00:10:02,478
Meemaw's got some outstanding
loans I need to pay back.

214
00:10:02,686 --> 00:10:04,438
I'm sorry,
I have to finish my homework

215
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:06,398
and then I have to help my dad.

216
00:10:08,275 --> 00:10:09,275
Come on.

217
00:10:09,693 --> 00:10:10,944
I'm your meemaw.

218
00:10:11,487 --> 00:10:12,613
I make you cookies.

219
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:14,281
How 'bout a little quid pro quo?

220
00:10:14,490 --> 00:10:15,490
As much as I enjoy

221
00:10:15,657 --> 00:10:17,785
your use of Latin, no.

222
00:10:19,161 --> 00:10:20,621
Shelly, time to get ready
for bed.

223
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:21,997
But I'm not done.

224
00:10:22,206 --> 00:10:23,624
Don't you sass me, too,
young man.

225
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:25,167
Brush your teeth and get to bed.

226
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:32,633
I think your anger might be
a little misdirected.

227
00:10:32,841 --> 00:10:34,134
Don't you start with me either.

228
00:10:34,593 --> 00:10:37,221
Now, see,
you're still shootin' wide.

229
00:10:46,647 --> 00:10:48,065
Good evening, Mrs. Cooper.

230
00:10:48,273 --> 00:10:49,273
Can I speak to Sheldon?

231
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:50,639
No, you can't speak to Sheldon.

232
00:10:50,734 --> 00:10:52,361
It's late. He's in bed.

233
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:55,531
Oh. I was hoping he might like
to go to a party with me.

234
00:10:55,739 --> 00:10:57,616
Has everyone lost their mind?

235
00:10:57,825 --> 00:10:59,409
He's a little boy, tam!

236
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:00,661
Good night!

237
00:11:02,037 --> 00:11:05,707
Good lord, that mouth of yours
is a machine gun tonight.

238
00:11:11,797 --> 00:11:13,048
What are you doing?

239
00:11:13,382 --> 00:11:15,467
Trying to calculate
the odds of the dolphins

240
00:11:15,676 --> 00:11:17,719
covering the spread next Sunday.

241
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:18,970
I like dolphins.

242
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:21,431
They talk out of that hole
in their head.

243
00:11:23,809 --> 00:11:24,434
Hello.

244
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:25,643
Tam?

245
00:11:29,314 --> 00:11:30,314
What are you doing here?

246
00:11:30,482 --> 00:11:32,109
Would you like to go
to a party with me?

247
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,957
I don't want to go to a party
with anyone.

248
00:11:33,986 --> 00:11:34,986
I would!

249
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:35,904
Please, Sheldon.

250
00:11:36,113 --> 00:11:37,489
It's right across the street.

251
00:11:37,698 --> 00:11:39,533
Just get me in,
and you can go back to bed.

252
00:11:39,950 --> 00:11:41,410
I have to ask my mom.

253
00:11:41,618 --> 00:11:43,412
No need.
She knows all about the party.

254
00:11:45,372 --> 00:11:46,707
All right, then.

255
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,458
I need a minute to change.

256
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:55,299
- Why are you wearing that?
- It makes me look older.

257
00:11:56,592 --> 00:11:58,873
Just so
we're clear, once you get in,

258
00:11:58,927 --> 00:12:00,387
I'm going home.

259
00:12:01,513 --> 00:12:02,806
Hey! Sheldon!

260
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:04,183
What are you doing?

261
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:06,991
Hey, everybody, check
it out! Sheldon's here!

262
00:12:10,939 --> 00:12:13,108
I hope that doesn't
wake up the kids.

263
00:12:13,317 --> 00:12:14,669
Should I go over there
and say something?

264
00:12:14,693 --> 00:12:15,693
I think you should.

265
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:18,906
I was bluffin'.

266
00:12:19,573 --> 00:12:21,241
Don't make me
put my socks back on.

267
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:23,243
Never mind.

268
00:12:23,452 --> 00:12:24,661
Good night.

269
00:12:26,205 --> 00:12:27,289
Good night.

270
00:12:35,172 --> 00:12:37,049
I feel bad about
yelling at Georgie.

271
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,259
He deserved it.

272
00:12:39,635 --> 00:12:40,844
You should do it more.

273
00:12:41,136 --> 00:12:42,429
I think he's feeling left out

274
00:12:42,638 --> 00:12:45,224
now that you and Sheldon are
spending so much time together.

275
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:50,771
Are you kiddin' me?
You're always saying to find

276
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:52,081
something in common
with Sheldon.

277
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:54,125
And now that I have, you're
telling me I'm ignoring Georgie?

278
00:12:54,149 --> 00:12:55,734
I'm not saying that.

279
00:12:55,943 --> 00:12:57,611
I'm just reminding you

280
00:12:57,819 --> 00:12:59,112
that you got two sons.

281
00:12:59,321 --> 00:13:00,530
I know.

282
00:13:02,199 --> 00:13:04,284
I also got a daughter
I need to spend more time with.

283
00:13:04,493 --> 00:13:05,493
You do.

284
00:13:06,203 --> 00:13:07,443
But I wouldn't worry about her.

285
00:13:07,621 --> 00:13:08,997
She's an angel.

286
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:16,838
- - Yeah, Sheldon!
- Put me down!

287
00:13:17,047 --> 00:13:19,549
I said put me down!

288
00:13:19,758 --> 00:13:21,402
Sheldon: Put me down!
I'm not enjoying this!

289
00:13:21,426 --> 00:13:23,095
Missy, what are you doing here?!

290
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,097
Cuttin' loose.
What are you doing here?

291
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:26,431
Sheldon: Slowly! Slowly!

292
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:27,683
Slowly!

293
00:13:29,101 --> 00:13:30,101
You, too?!

294
00:13:30,269 --> 00:13:31,603
Hello, Georgie!

295
00:13:31,812 --> 00:13:33,230
You're not supposed to be here.

296
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,607
Neither are you!
You're grounded!

297
00:13:37,025 --> 00:13:37,651
Come on.

298
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:39,486
Both of you are going home. Now.

299
00:13:39,695 --> 00:13:41,863
- Oh, thank goodness.
- Aw.

300
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:46,535
How's puberty treating you?

301
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:48,787
Because it is
knocking me for a loop.

302
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:51,872
Right?

303
00:13:58,505 --> 00:14:00,465
Adult Sheldon: Somehow,
my parents didn't find out

304
00:14:00,632 --> 00:14:02,509
about me partying heartily.

305
00:14:02,801 --> 00:14:03,969
But I did pay a price

306
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:06,596
for burning the candle
at both ends.

307
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:09,224
Imade a mistake on a math test.

308
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:12,728
In my exhaustion,
I did all the calculations

309
00:14:12,936 --> 00:14:13,936
in my head,

310
00:14:14,021 --> 00:14:17,566
and, like a common zoo animal,
forgot to show my work.

311
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:20,694
I just saw one of those girls
from the party,

312
00:14:20,902 --> 00:14:23,238
and she acknowledged
my existence by doing this.

313
00:14:24,281 --> 00:14:25,741
I've never felt so alive.

314
00:14:29,161 --> 00:14:30,161
Are you okay?

315
00:14:31,288 --> 00:14:32,288
No, I'm not.

316
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:35,709
Yeah, so?

317
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:39,171
A b-plus... that's
the beginning of the end.

318
00:14:39,588 --> 00:14:40,672
The end of what?

319
00:14:40,881 --> 00:14:41,923
My life.

320
00:14:42,132 --> 00:14:44,718
If I don't make some changes,
who knows how far I'll fall.

321
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:48,221
I could wind up a drug addict,
or a lawyer.

322
00:14:48,430 --> 00:14:50,140
Is it possible
you're overreacting?

323
00:14:50,474 --> 00:14:54,269
No. Starting today, I'm done
helping the football team.

324
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:58,482
But if you do that, girls will
no longer greet me like this.

325
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:00,901
I'll greet you like that.

326
00:15:02,361 --> 00:15:03,904
It's not the same.

327
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,908
Adult Sheldon: Extricating
myself from this situation

328
00:15:08,116 --> 00:15:09,951
was not going to be easy.

329
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:13,622
My father was counting on me,
meemaw was counting on me,

330
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:15,832
the school was counting on me.

331
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:18,460
After much thought,
I decided to employ

332
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:22,172
the one strategic maneuver
I knew I could count on.

333
00:15:22,464 --> 00:15:23,464
I tattled.

334
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:24,590
Mom?

335
00:15:28,136 --> 00:15:29,554
J'j'

336
00:15:30,514 --> 00:15:33,433
j” robbin' people
with a six-gun j”

337
00:15:33,642 --> 00:15:36,186
j” I fought the law
and the law won... j”

338
00:15:36,395 --> 00:15:39,439
Sheldon got a b-plus!
That's terrible for him!

339
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:42,442
I'm very disappointed
in all three of you.

340
00:15:42,651 --> 00:15:45,404
That is right. Missy, this
is for your ballet class.

341
00:15:45,612 --> 00:15:48,156
We do not go to parties.

342
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:50,158
I am very disappointed.

343
00:15:56,123 --> 00:15:57,123
Hey.

344
00:15:58,333 --> 00:15:58,959
Got to go pick up

345
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:01,087
some equipment for the team;
You want to join me?

346
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,921
Can't. I'm grounded.

347
00:16:03,672 --> 00:16:05,340
Yeah, well...

348
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:06,842
I won't tell if you won't.

349
00:16:09,678 --> 00:16:10,804
Sheldon going?

350
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,098
That little snitch?
Absolutely not.

351
00:16:19,271 --> 00:16:20,981
Sheldon still gonna
help you with the math?

352
00:16:21,189 --> 00:16:22,482
I don't think so.

353
00:16:23,066 --> 00:16:25,152
But I did hear his little
Asian friend can do it.

354
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:35,911
Hey.

355
00:16:36,371 --> 00:16:37,371
Hello.

356
00:16:37,706 --> 00:16:38,706
So...

357
00:16:39,124 --> 00:16:41,376
Oilers are a four-point favorite
for this Sunday's game,

358
00:16:41,585 --> 00:16:45,172
but it's a home game, so I'm
thinking I give the points.

359
00:16:46,047 --> 00:16:47,215
What do you think?

360
00:16:47,883 --> 00:16:49,968
I think I have
to tell on you again.

361
00:16:50,177 --> 00:16:52,637
Go ahead. What's your
mama gonna do, ground me?

362
00:16:56,766 --> 00:16:58,768
Take the oilers,
give the points.

363
00:17:00,061 --> 00:17:03,064
I love you, moonpie.

364
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:08,778
Adult Sheldon: For the record,
the oilers lost that game

365
00:17:08,987 --> 00:17:10,822
by four touchdowns.

366
00:17:11,239 --> 00:17:13,742
Meemaw never asked
for my advice again.

367
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:20,790
Come on, come on,
come on. Damn it!

368
00:17:21,041 --> 00:17:22,041
Okay.

369
00:17:22,834 --> 00:17:24,044
One more time.

370
00:17:25,462 --> 00:17:27,547
Mama needs a new jet ski!

371
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:28,839
And...

372
00:17:28,882 --> 00:17:30,091
Rat bastard!

373
00:17:32,427 --> 00:17:33,803
How you doin' there, Connie?

374
00:17:35,055 --> 00:17:36,932
Hey, Vincent.

375
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,725
What brings you to Louisiana?

376
00:17:38,934 --> 00:17:39,935
Wait, don't tell me.

377
00:17:40,143 --> 00:17:41,645
You're here to see Tony Orlando.

378
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:43,146
'Fraid not.

379
00:17:43,355 --> 00:17:44,795
Oh, well, you ought
to check him out.

380
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:47,192
He'll, uh, knock your socks off.

381
00:17:47,442 --> 00:17:48,902
I like my socks on.

382
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:52,864
Connie, you're putting me
in a very awkward position.

383
00:17:54,157 --> 00:17:55,617
I won a toaster oven
playing keno.

384
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:56,867
You want it?

385
00:17:58,328 --> 00:17:59,329
I got one.

386
00:18:00,205 --> 00:18:01,414
I want my money.

387
00:18:01,623 --> 00:18:03,166
All right.

388
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:04,668
Hang on.

389
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:08,004
That's a very nice jacket.

390
00:18:08,213 --> 00:18:09,589
You're looking dapper.

391
00:18:13,552 --> 00:18:14,928
Ah.

392
00:18:15,387 --> 00:18:16,721
Hey, they comp my room here.

393
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:18,014
They do that for you?

394
00:18:18,348 --> 00:18:20,892
Actually, they frown
upon my presence here.

395
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:25,146
Oh. I also get a coupon
for the breakfast buffet.

396
00:18:25,355 --> 00:18:26,523
You should look into that.

397
00:18:30,652 --> 00:18:31,652
Constance!

398
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:33,697
Patience, Vincenzo.

399
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:40,620
Yes!

400
00:18:40,829 --> 00:18:42,372
Oh!

401
00:18:42,581 --> 00:18:44,499
All right, now we 're talking.

402
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:46,710
Will you take a down payment
in quarters?

403
00:18:46,918 --> 00:18:48,003
Do I have a choice?

404
00:18:49,546 --> 00:18:50,839
Start scoopin'.

405
00:18:51,256 --> 00:18:52,674
I got to go see Tony Orlando.

406
00:18:58,805 --> 00:18:59,806
Oof.

407
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:09,898
Hey!

408
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,611
Hey, I need another cup!

